#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keyring is out of date \\X'tty: link https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/issues/2213'I<\\%#2213>\\X'tty: link'"
msgstr "Inelul de chei este dezactualizat \\X'tty: link https://github.com/archlinux/archinstall/issues/2213'I<\\%#2213>\\X'tty: link'"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Missing key-issues tend to be that the \\X'tty: link https://archlinux.org/"
"packages/core/any/archlinux-keyring/'I<\\%archlinux-keyring>\\X'tty: link' "
"package is out of date, usually as a result of an outdated ISO.  There is an "
"attempt from upstream to fix this issue, and it\\(aqs the \\X'tty: link "
"https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/archlinux-keyring/-/blob/"
"7e672dad10652a80d1cc575d75cdb46442cd7f96/wkd_sync/archlinux-keyring-wkd-"
"sync.service.in'I<\\%archlinux-keyring-wkd-sync.service>\\X'tty: link'"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"The service starts almost immediately during boot, and if network is not "
"configured in time — the service will fail.  Subsequently the B<archinstall> "
"run might operate on a old keyring despite there being an update service for "
"this."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"There is really no way to reliably over time work around this issue in "
"B<archinstall>\\&.  Instead, efforts to the upstream service should be "
"considered the way forward. And/or keys not expiring between a sane amount "
"of ISO\\(aqs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"The issue can happen on new ISO\\(aqs too even as little as a few days after "
"release, as some keys might expire right after the keyring is I<\"burnt "
"in\"> to the ISO."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"Another common issue relating to the network not being configured, is that "
"time might not be set correctly - resulting in the keyring not being able to "
"update. See I<\\%Waiting for time sync #2144>\\&."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux
#, no-wrap
msgid "AUR packages"
msgstr "Pachete AUR"

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux
msgid ""
"This is also a catch-all issue.  \\X'tty: link https://wiki.archlinux.org/"
"title/Arch_User_Repository#Updating_packages'I<\\%AUR is "
"unsupported>\\X'tty: link', and until that changes we cannot use AUR "
"packages to solve feature requests in B<archinstall>\\&."
